A killed tsc leaves tsconfig_*.tsbuildinfo behind. The next run sees
that file, decides the inputs are unchanged, and exits 0 without
writing the .js and .d.ts outputs. GN then treats the action as done.
Later targets fail with TS2307 because the path mapping points at an
empty tsc/ directory.

ts_library.py already deletes the .tsbuildinfo after a successful
tsc, because GN decides freshness. Delete it before tsc as well, so a
file left by a killed compiler cannot suppress emit. This showed up
when the Studio rebooted during the TypeScript actions.

--- a/tools/typescript/ts_library.py
+++ b/tools/typescript/ts_library.py
@@ -275,6 +275,15 @@
           if os.path.exists(to_check):
             os.remove(to_check)
 
+  # A killed tsc can leave .tsbuildinfo without outputs. The next tsc
+  # then exits 0 and emits nothing. GN already decides which target is
+  # dirty, so the incremental file is only a hazard. The finally block
+  # below removes it again after a successful run.
+  if args.composite:
+    tsbuildinfo_path = os.path.join(args.gen_dir, tsbuildinfo_name)
+    if os.path.exists(tsbuildinfo_path):
+      os.remove(tsbuildinfo_path)
+
   try:
     node.RunNode([
         node_modules.PathToTypescript(), '--project',
